    "q-161550": {
      "dom_id": "step-q161550",
      "name": "Question 3",
      "problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/differential/14261151/assets/d3ded2a039746e3c8f7a7ee4afb70b0d697468d1aee8f0e9dab24b1ca87897d2.png)\n\nConsider the set $A,$ shown above. The boundary of $A$ is given by\n\n$$\n∂A=\\{(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,\\bbox[5px,border:1px solid black]{\\phantom{AAAAA}}\\,\\}.\n$$\n\nWhat is the missing expression?",
      "worked_solution": "The boundary of a set $A,$ denoted $∂A,$ is the set that contains all the boundary points of $A.$\n\nThe set $A$ and its boundary $∂A$ are shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/differential/14261151/assets/d1946cea37f202705e6517ba760afa6617075f748901b10588ea98628a3e9e50.png)\n\nFrom the diagram, the boundary points of $A$ lie on the parabola $2y={x}^{2}.$\n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\n∂A=\\{(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,2y={x}^{2}\\,\\}.\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
